I was playing version 1.0.2 of hack, and had a very interesting
experience.  Can anybody explain what I should have done?

I was in a shopkeepers (used armor) shop, and when I dropped items that
I owned, the shopkeeper appropriated them.  If I picked them back up,
they were listed as unpaid.  In addition, even when I had no unpaid
items (checked by means of the Iu command), the shopkeeper would not let
me out of the shop.  Eventually a Mimic and a Giant Ant came in, and so
I tried to fight them for a while.  When this appeared hopeless, I gave
up and attacked to shopkeeper, figuring that I was dead anyway.  The
shopkeeper killed me, and then took "the 45 zordniks that I owed him".
What was going on here?  How could I have satisfied the shopkeeper that
I didn't owe him anything, or give him what he wanted, when it became
clear that he wasn't going to let me out of the shop?

By the way, listing my inventory (i command) did not show any such thing
as zordniks.  I have never heard of zordniks before.  I was a tourist on
level 6, with approx. 45 HP.  Any help would be appreciated.

